        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "db3f726c5f12dcac",
      "text": "Under pressure to help businesses and workers cope with soaring fuel prices, the French government has announced it will expand targeted energy relief for those most affected.  The new measures will cost €450 million, bringing the total so far to €1.4 billion. Meanwhile, as French president Emmanuel Macron calls for allowing more biofuels to be added to diesel, we speak with an expert on the potential environmental impact of a rapid ramp-up in biofuel use.",
      "title": "French government scales up targeted fuel price relief",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-french-government-scales-up-targeted-fuel-price-relief",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T20:54:51.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "445b0d118f51b36e",
      "text": "A viral NATO video is being falsely framed online as “war propaganda”, with users accusing the Alliance of sharing a “promotional video” designed to prepare the public for imminent war with Russia. But the footage is not new: NATO published it in July 2024 for its 75th anniversary, and it’s been stripped of its original context. The claim comes as European leaders warn of growing Russian hybrid threats, including alleged drone, cyber and sabotage activity. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.",
      "title": "Viral NATO video falsely framed as ‘war propaganda’ against Russia",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T20:44:29.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7c7000ae161bb983",
      "text": "In tonight's edition, the United States is withholding a visa for Sudanese army chief al-Burhan ahead of his scheduled UN appearance. Also, Ghana’s beefing up its drugs authority in the wake of  major drug busts in France, Belgium and South Africa. And it’s back-to-school season in Ivory Coast.",
      "title": "US refusing to give Sudan's de facto leader visa for UN",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/us-refusing-to-give-sudan-s-de-facto-leader-visa-for-un",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T20:13:30.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "64285ee15c42a6e8",
      "text": "French President Emmanuel Macron used his last address before the UN General Assembly as France's leader to urge the world's nations to stand alongside the United Nations in the face of a resurgent \"law of the jungle\". Macron also called for a moratorium on strikes on civilian and energy infrastructure in the Russia-Ukraine war and an \"open-source\" model for frontier AI independent of China and the US.",
      "title": "Macron urges world to 'stand firm' against 'abuse of power by empires' in final UN speech",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260922-macron-urges-world-stand-firm-against-abuse-of-power-by-empires-final-un-speech",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T20:08:28.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "aff2f98ded6b0299",
      "text": "A year ago, Donald Trump went to the rostrum of the United Nations General Assembly - and after taxing an axe to US aid and development funding, read the world the riot act. One Iran war later, the US president sticking to script with a speech that borrowed much of the language of last year. With citizens on five continents now feeling the pain at the pump, we'll ask what it will take to tame a global energy crisis whose potential spiral mirrors the contagion of hostilities from the Strait of Hormuz to the mouth of the Red Sea?",
      "title": "Trump's world? Leaders navigate consequences of US policy",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-trump-s-world-leaders-navigate-consequences-of-us-policy",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:14:41.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c6deb421f1d83b43",
      "text": "🔴Watch live: French President Emmanuel Macron addresses UN General Assembly",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T17:41:33.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9a2daf21ab939c15",
      "text": "US President Donald Trump launched a full-throated defence of the deeply unpopular US-Israeli war against Iran before the UN General Assembly on Tuesday, claiming that Washington would reach a deal with Tehran after the upcoming US midterm elections. Trump also rejected the idea of global regulation of artificial intelligence, said the government of Cuba would soon \"fall\", and urged member countries of the International Criminal Court to \"resign\".",
      "title": "Iran, AI and the ICC: Trump makes threats, touts policies at UN General Assembly",
      "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-iran-ai-and-the-icc-trump-makes-threats-touts-policies-un-general-assembly",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T17:09:26.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "France 24 [T2]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c6deb421f1d83b43",
