      "id": "5714113c1acb6d0d",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Accra Reset’s report states countries in the region and global south should take greater control of their health development after USAID debacle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The United States’ withdrawal from key aid programs has put healthcare in Africa and the Global South “under growing strain” a new report warns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The report says the Trump administration’s cuts to programs such as US Agency for International Development (USAID), as well as the Covid-19 pandemic and rising costs of living globally have brought “new urgency” for the need to reform healthcare in the region.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/21/africa-healthcare-aid-program-withdrawl\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Healthcare in Africa ‘under growing strain’ after US withdrawal from aid programs, report warns",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/21/africa-healthcare-aid-program-withdrawl",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T22:33:40.000Z",
