      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4d3023158a272a09",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;After a plane journey in shackles, an Iranian woman found herself in the middle of Africa in a country she did not know existed. She is one of thousands deported from the US on the back of shadowy deals made with dozens of countries. An in-depth investigation reveals the ‘show of force’ costing American taxpayers millions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;No one would tell the shackled detainees onboard the US immigration plane where they were going. The officers in charge would taunt them when they asked, they said. It was only when the seat-back video screens finally showed a map that the 18 migrants worked it out.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/sep/21/trump-deportation-deals\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Banished to alien lands: Trump’s secret deportation deals",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/sep/21/trump-deportation-deals",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T05:00:38.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c26acc91ebbc6922",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Group trapped at Hotel Bamy after US removal as rights groups sound alarm over poor conditions and violence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two men that the Trump administration expelled to Equatorial Guinea were bound, fitted with bags over their heads, beaten and pushed down a flight of stairs, all in plain view of other US deportees, according to witnesses and human rights lawyers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The men – one from Egypt and one from Eritrea – were then taken to a prison. About 30 detainees from the US remain trapped at a hotel in the outskirts of the coastal city of Malabo after being deported from the US. Detainees have said they believe the men were beaten for telling the press and human rights advocates about the poor conditions and violence inside the hotel, and that they are haunted by flashbacks and terrified they will be retaliated against next.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/18/us-men-deported-hotel-equatorial-guinea\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Men deported from US bound and beaten in Equatorial Guinea detention hotel, lawyers say",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/18/us-men-deported-hotel-equatorial-guinea",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-18T23:08:49.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1269431bccc0ac9a",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Police fire teargas as protests break out in city of Minna after deaths of suspected illegal goldminers, many of whom were children&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Survivors from a prison cell in Nigeria where 37 suspected illegal goldminers died while in the custody of a paramilitary group this week have recounted their panic and struggle for breath, as police on Friday fired teargas at people protesting against the deaths and imposed an overnight curfew in the city of Minna.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The victims – many of whom were children – were found dead on Thursday in the cells of the Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps (NSCDC), which had raided suspected illegal goldmines and ⁠locked up dozens of miners in the city, the state capital of the mineral-rich state of Niger.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/18/survivor-panic-struggle-breathe-nigeria-prison-cell-died-minna\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Survivors recount panic and struggle to breathe in Nigerian prison cell where 37 died",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/18/survivor-panic-struggle-breathe-nigeria-prison-cell-died-minna",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-18T17:27:39.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f35415b47e261567",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Four of Nusrat Osman’s alleged abductors were killed during rescue after she was taken from outside her home last week&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A British woman kidnapped in Malawi last week has been rescued by police after a shootout in which four of her alleged abductors were killed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nusrat Osman was abducted outside her home in the southern city of Blantyre on 11 September at about 12.30pm. Police had &lt;a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/malawipolice/posts/pfbid02SgvBBVEhDbZA4RnTDfUFe8ethHvTrZKKS11jX9TpEykmB8RAwA27cWqntNHMw2M2l\"&gt;offered a reward&lt;/a&gt; of 30m Malawi kwacha (£12,950) for information leading to her rescue and the arrest of the perpetrators.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/18/british-woman-kidnapped-malawi-police-shootout\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "British woman who was kidnapped in Malawi rescued by police after shootout",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/18/british-woman-kidnapped-malawi-police-shootout",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-18T11:21:36.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3214054e9846d68c",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;The move comes after Jamaica’s culture minister Olivia Grange travelled to the UK earlier this month to lodge the historic petition&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;King Charles has referred a landmark slavery reparations petition from Jamaica to a high-level UK appeals court for legal advice, Jamaica’s culture minister announced in parliament on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Referring to the move as a “really big deal”, &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/sep/09/jamaica-slavery-reparations-king-charles\"&gt;Olivia Grange&lt;/a&gt; told Jamaica’s MPs the monarch had confirmed that their legal questions have been passed on to the London-based privy council – the final court of appeal for UK overseas territories and some Commonwealth countries.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/jamaica-king-charles-to-refer-slavery-reparations-petition-to-privy-council\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Jamaica hails King’s decision to refer slavery reparations petition to privy council as ‘really big deal’",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/jamaica-king-charles-to-refer-slavery-reparations-petition-to-privy-council",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T01:15:26.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "121129b9a99726ed",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Polo, with sustained winds of 165mph, is churning 215 miles south of Zihuatanejo but is unlikely to directly hit Mexico&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A tropical storm off the south-west coast of &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico\"&gt;Mexico&lt;/a&gt; has intensified into a category 5 monster in fewer than 24 hours, fueled by stronger than usual &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/elnino\"&gt;El Niño&lt;/a&gt; weather patterns in the Pacific Ocean.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/#Polo\"&gt;Hurricane Polo&lt;/a&gt; was sending out maximum sustained winds of 165mph (266km/h) on Tuesday as its center churned about 215 miles (346km) south of the coastal city of Zihuatanejo, in Guerrero state.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/hurricane-polo-mexico\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Hurricane Polo, rapidly intensifying from strong El Niño patterns, rages off coast of Mexico",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/hurricane-polo-mexico",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T19:09:29.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0fb7282fae73bec2",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;US president may have upstaged the ghost of Soviet leader Khrushchev by musing destruction of fellow member state&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Donald Trump has a habit of discomfiting delegates to the United Nations general assembly. But this year, he may have upstaged the ghost of Nikita Khrushchev by openly contemplating the annihilation of a fellow UN member state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Eleven minutes into a 40-minute address, the US president announced he had “a big decision to make” over Iran, which has staged a much more determined resistance than Trump anticipated when he decided to go to war against the country in February.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/donald-trump-unga-speech\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Trump’s threat to annihilate Iran to UN general assembly is stunning, even for him",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/donald-trump-unga-speech",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:23:08.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "902b64cf7693ec10",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Canadian province alleges deadly attack could have been prevented if  company had warned police of shooter’s ChatGPT use&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;British Columbia has sued &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/openai\"&gt;OpenAI&lt;/a&gt;, saying a mass shooting at a school in the Canadian province could have been prevented if the company had warned local ⁠law enforcement that the shooter ⁠had used ChatGPT to ​plan the attack.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The lawsuit, filed in &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/san-francisco\"&gt;San Francisco&lt;/a&gt; federal court on Monday, names OpenAI and its CEO, &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/sam-altman\"&gt;Sam Altman&lt;/a&gt;, as defendants. It is seeking damages to fund recovery efforts in the province after the February attack, as well as an order directing changes to the way the company handles ChatGPT conversations that could lead to violence.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/22/british-columbia-sues-openai-sam-altman-tumbler-ridge-school-shooting\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "British Columbia sues OpenAI and Sam Altman over Tumbler Ridge mass school shooting",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/22/british-columbia-sues-openai-sam-altman-tumbler-ridge-school-shooting",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T04:29:22.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "adc6f82ada8b2d8c",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Wildfire forces evacuations and burns through mountains surrounding Villa de Leyva in the north-east &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Colombian authorities declared a public calamity as a wildfire burned through mountains surrounding one of the country’s best-known colonial towns in the north-east, scorching large swaths of vegetation and forcing evacuations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Nearly 20 active fires are burning across the South American country. Dry conditions have increased fire danger in Colombia as it braces for the effects of El Niño, which can help wildfires spread.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/colombia-wildfire-villa-de-leyva\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Colombia declares public calamity as wildfire threatens popular tourist area",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/colombia-wildfire-villa-de-leyva",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T17:13:23.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9657340adce9be1c",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Lian Yunzhi solves 3x3 puzzle on several occasions in average time of under 4.5 seconds, according to state media&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A six-year-old &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/china\"&gt;Chinese&lt;/a&gt; girl has set a new women’s world record for solving a Rubik’s Cube in just over four seconds, state media reported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;“Speedcuber” Lian Yunzhi broke the women’s 3x3 average world record twice this month at two World Cube Association certified competitions in Wuhan and Guangzhou, according to state broadcaster CCTV on Monday.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/games/2026/sep/22/six-year-old-chinese-girl-rubiks-cube-world-record-lian-yunzhi\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Six-year-old Chinese girl ‘sets new women’s Rubik’s Cube world record’",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2026/sep/22/six-year-old-chinese-girl-rubiks-cube-world-record-lian-yunzhi",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:10:53.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "89b0911bfc147a44",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Disappearance of jet components sparks concern some of the program’s technology secrets could have been exposed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/22/anthony-albanese-new-york-united-nations-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\"&gt;Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get our &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;breaking news email&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"&gt;free app&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;daily news podcast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Department of Defence is examining how F-35 fighter jet parts bound for the US from Australia were unexpectedly diverted to Hong Kong, the acting prime minister, Richard Marles, has said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marles said “very much everything that has occurred at the Australian end” would be reviewed, but claimed the technology parts were not “sensitive”, as &lt;a href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/2026/09/18/congress-f-35-china-investigation-01083647\"&gt;first reported by Politico over the weekend&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/australia-investigating-how-f-35-fighter-jet-parts-bound-for-us-went-missing-in-hong-kong\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Australia investigating how F-35 fighter jet parts bound for US went missing in Hong Kong",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/australia-investigating-how-f-35-fighter-jet-parts-bound-for-us-went-missing-in-hong-kong",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:00:15.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d95d679cabd8bb73",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Rescuers search for missing in collapsed homes after storm causes landslides, travel chaos and power outages&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Typhoon Dujuan has killed at least four people and injured 22 in Japan, while tens of thousands of houses near Tokyo remained without power after the storm swept through the region, authorities said on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dujuan – which &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/21/weather-tracker-japan-typhoon-dujuan\"&gt;brought violent winds of 144km/h (89mph)&lt;/a&gt; – was moving away from Japan on Tuesday morning, allowing authorities to downgrade most heavy rain and landslide warnings.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/typhoon-dujuan-japan-latest-weather-millions-told-to-evacuate-tokyo\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "At least four people killed in Japan as typhoon Dujuan triggers heavy rain, landslides",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/typhoon-dujuan-japan-latest-weather-millions-told-to-evacuate-tokyo",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T04:48:59.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "eb68ad731beb3f2f",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Storm system expected to hit Izu Islands as it strengthens. Meanwhile, Atlantic hurricane season is unusually quiet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tropical Storm Dujuan is skirting the coast of Japan and despite avoiding a direct landfall, is still expected to leave its mark. Dujuan briefly reached typhoon status on Friday before weakening to a tropical storm again on Sunday morning. But it is expected to restrengthen back to a typhoon by Tuesday morning. Sustained winds could reach 80mph (129km/h), with gusts approaching 100mph.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although mainland Japan has avoided a direct hit, Dujuan’s track takes it across the Izu Islands, where evacuation warnings are in place. Heavy rain, flooding and landslide alerts are widespread, with high waves adding another threat to exposed coastal areas and islands.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/21/weather-tracker-japan-typhoon-dujuan\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Japanese islands brace for Dujuan to become a typhoon again",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/21/weather-tracker-japan-typhoon-dujuan",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T09:45:49.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff814897f8dec758",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Beijing believes slowdown calls aim to lock in US advantage, and is pursuing a different balance between safety and pace&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/ng-interactive/2026/sep/19/china-ai-foreign-policy-dario-amodei\"&gt;China bogeyman looms large over American firms’ AI doomsday scenario&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;About two years ago, education entrepreneur Boris But had what he calls a “penny-drop moment” – that, like countless others in China, his company needed to embrace AI before it was made obsolete by it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;His clients, well-off parents looking to send their children to study overseas, had begun arriving in his office reeling off information and opinions gleaned not from rival firms, but from chatbots.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/20/why-china-is-pushing-back-on-us-warnings-over-rapid-ai-development\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Why China is pushing back on US warnings over rapid AI development",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/20/why-china-is-pushing-back-on-us-warnings-over-rapid-ai-development",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-20T06:00:09.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c20ab414ca4ca164",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Follow the day’s news live&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get our &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;breaking news email&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"&gt;free app&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;daily news podcast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Andrew Bragg&lt;/strong&gt;, the shadow housing minister, said he believes in “big debates” about housing after pushing his new proposal yesterday to allow people to use their superannuation as collateral to get a home loan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The policy hasn’t been adopted by the opposition, and leader &lt;strong&gt;Angus Taylor &lt;/strong&gt;said yesterday it wasn’t Coalition policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re a great country, and we should be able to have big debates, as we had in the 80s and 90s about national savings and housing and the like, which led, in fact, to the super guarantee. …&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It’s very important that we look to calibrate the retirement and housing and superannuation systems to make sure that they’re getting the best outcomes for the Australian people.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/23/anthony-albanese-un-assembly-ai-social-media-labor-coalition-abc-four-corners-ntwnfb\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Australia news live: Gus Lamont’s parents make emotional plea for information; NAB customers report online banking outage",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/23/anthony-albanese-un-assembly-ai-social-media-labor-coalition-abc-four-corners-ntwnfb",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T06:49:30.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8d2430a8ea095e31",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Several measures were previously introduced or supported by Coalition, prompting claim Liberals and Nationals would ‘let climate change rip’&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/23/anthony-albanese-un-assembly-ai-social-media-labor-coalition-abc-four-corners-ntwnfb\"&gt;Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get our &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;breaking news email&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"&gt;free app&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;daily news podcast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Angus Taylor has vowed to repeal a raft of emissions reduction and renewable energy policies, including several measures supported by or introduced under past Coalition governments, within a month of being elected prime minister, prompting accusations he would “let climate change rip”.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Wednesday, Taylor’s energy spokesperson, Dan Tehan, announced a new bill would be introduced to parliament within 30 days after a Coalition win at the next federal election to ensure affordable, reliable and secure energy to Australians.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scrap &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/feb/18/carmakers-face-possible-heavy-fines-in-australia-for-failing-to-meet-climate-targets\"&gt;vehicle emissions standards&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remove the legislated net zero by 2050 target.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Revoke four of six offshore wind energy zones due for completion by the late 2030s: the Hunter, Illawarra, Southern Ocean and Bunbury regions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Introduce a renewable energy code of conduct for developers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Require energy funding provided to states and territories prioritises energy affordability and reliability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Change the Australian Energy Regulator’s main focus to affordability and reliability.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/23/angus-taylor-pledges-to-repeal-swathe-of-climate-policies-saying-australia-has-done-its-bit\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Angus Taylor pledges to repeal swathe of climate policies, saying ‘Australia has done its bit’",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/23/angus-taylor-pledges-to-repeal-swathe-of-climate-policies-saying-australia-has-done-its-bit",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T06:45:12.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b6431a5d611d12bf",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;The singer, songwriter, actor and advocate, who has died following a cardiac arrest while touring in Europe, kept his band’s flame burning until the end&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Angry Anderson has died aged 79, after he was hospitalised following a cardiac arrest while on tour in Germany with the band Rose Tattoo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gary Anderson was not a nice boy growing up. As one of the founding members of Melbourne motorcycle club the Vigilanties, he initially earned the sobriquet Mouse, on account of his diminutive stature. Determined to prove himself a man, he developed a penchant for taking on blokes twice his size. It earned him a new nickname: the Angry Ant.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/sep/23/angry-anderson-dies-rose-tattoo-frontman-death-aged-79\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Angry Anderson dies aged 79: Rose Tattoo frontman was a ferocious rock ’n’ roll singer and youth advocate",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/sep/23/angry-anderson-dies-rose-tattoo-frontman-death-aged-79",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T06:32:04.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3cf1ba64ddd6c210",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Inquiry investigating allegations of corruption and criminal conduct on state’s $150bn pipeline of infrastructure projects to leave ‘no stone unturned’&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/23/anthony-albanese-un-assembly-ai-social-media-labor-coalition-abc-four-corners-ntwnfb\"&gt;Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get our &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;breaking news email&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"&gt;free app&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;daily news podcast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;The opening public hearing of the royal commission into Victoria’s Big Build has shown Jacinta Allan knew of allegations the construction union allowed criminals and bikies on to state projects as early as 2023.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It was also revealed that the inquiry – officially named the royal commission into the integrity of major public and civil infrastructure construction projects in Victoria – held “closed” hearings following &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/20/victorian-premier-to-call-royal-commission-into-construction-sector-amid-cfmeu-scandal-ntwnfb\"&gt;its launch in August&lt;/a&gt;, and plans to hold public hearings during the November state election campaign.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/23/victoria-big-build-royal-commission-construction-inquiry-corruption-first-hearing-ntwnfb\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Bikies, ‘moral compass malfunctions’ and corruption cost: Victoria’s Big Build royal commission holds first public hearing",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/23/victoria-big-build-royal-commission-construction-inquiry-corruption-first-hearing-ntwnfb",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:52:51.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f50e618f9e3a9a36",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Due to take off in 2028, it is set to be the national carrier’s second ultra long-haul route after Sydney to London&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/23/anthony-albanese-un-assembly-ai-social-media-labor-coalition-abc-four-corners-ntwnfb\"&gt;Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get our &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;breaking news email&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"&gt;free app&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"&gt;daily news podcast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Qantas says travellers will be able to fly between Sydney and New York in just 18 hours from mid-2028 when the airline launches its second ultra long-haul route, cutting at least three hours from the travel time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The route will be the second in Qantas’ Project Sunrise expansion plans, with new &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jun/18/qantas-delays-non-stop-flights-from-sydney-to-london-again\"&gt;Sydney to London direct flights&lt;/a&gt; planned for October 2027, after some delays.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/23/qantas-direct-flights-from-sydney-to-new-york\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Qantas announces 18-hour direct flights from Sydney to New York with onboard ‘wellbeing zones’",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/23/qantas-direct-flights-from-sydney-to-new-york",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:17:07.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "17fd077b59ecdfc1",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Lawyers for James ‘Fergie’ Chambers, wanted over alleged support for Hamas, say client is being persecuted&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Spanish government has decided to allow the Trump administration’s controversial extradition request to extradite wealthy activist James “Fergie” Chambers to continue in the country’s courts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chambers, a US citizen and wealthy donor to leftwing and humanitarian projects, is currently imprisoned in Madrid. It is the first known case of the US seeking to extradite a citizen over alleged support for Hamas, an accusation tied to money Chambers has donated to support Palestinians, including the &lt;a href=\"https://thesameerproject.org/\"&gt;Sameer Project,&lt;/a&gt; in Gaza.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/spain-extradition-request-james-fergie-chambers\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Spain allows US extradition case against pro-Palestine aid donor to proceed",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/spain-extradition-request-james-fergie-chambers",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T22:16:55.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9a72eec20b2e0d72",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman delisted in what Ireland’s EU presidency calls ‘a difficult compromise’ for the bloc&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The EU has agreed to remove two Russian billionaires, Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman, from its sanctions list, while extending restrictions on nearly 3,000 individuals and companies accused of supporting the war on Ukraine for the next three years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;With an end-of-Tuesday deadline looming to preserve the Russia blacklist, the EU’s 27 member states found a compromise that meant delisting the two oligarchs in spite of very few countries wanting this outcome. EU sanctions have to be approved unanimously.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/eu-removes-oligarchs-from-russia-sanctions-list-as-deadline-looms\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "EU removes two oligarchs from Russia sanctions list as deadline looms",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/eu-removes-oligarchs-from-russia-sanctions-list-as-deadline-looms",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T18:07:19.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "164f843cf4ce89d3",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Agreement signed at the UN general assembly in New York&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nordic correspondent &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emotions among Greenlanders are a mixture of hope, scepticism and fear ahead of the signing of a new much vaunted deal on Arctic security between the US, Greenland and Denmark.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;“There have been many different reactions in Greenland because &lt;strong&gt;they are talking about a deal but no one can see the deal,&lt;/strong&gt; we don’t know what it is all about, and what’s in it for us or what’s in it. Also, because we have been terrorised as a people for the last 1.5 years by the American president, so &lt;strong&gt;many people feel no trust at all.”&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/eu-trump-russia-putin-sanctions-ukraine-greenland-denmark-zelenskyy-latest-news-updates\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "US to build new military bases in Greenland as deal seeks to end tensions between Nato allies - as it happened",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/eu-trump-russia-putin-sanctions-ukraine-greenland-denmark-zelenskyy-latest-news-updates",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T16:51:13.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c371e43b91011425",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Officials say one pilot safely ejected as F-16 believed to have crashed on approach to Spangdahlem after training drill&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;⁠An F-16 fighter jet assigned to the US air ⁠base Spangdahlem ⁠in ​western Germany crashed on Tuesday, the US military said, ⁠adding that one pilot had ejected safely and was receiving ⁠medical treatment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The cause of the incident ​is under ‌investigation, the military ‌said in a statement, with ‌emergency response personnel at the scene of the crash.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/fighter-jet-crashes-germany\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "US fighter jet crashes at air base in western Germany",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/fighter-jet-crashes-germany",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T16:49:18.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9817f2a9e8859114",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Combination of Miuccia Prada with Belgian designer Raf Simons once again spins gold for fashion house&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Miuccia Prada’s style formula is simple: begin with a great skirt. Her personal uniform is a knee-length skirt, A-line or pleated, most often with a plain sweater and kitten heels.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Prada collection that opened Milan fashion week made a compelling case for her favourite outfit, with a skirt the star of every one of the 63 looks – no dresses, no trousers. It won the room over, so expect to see the personality skirt on a high street near you soon.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2026/sep/22/skirts-miuccia-prada-raf-simons-milan-fashion-week\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Skirts given star billing as Prada swerves trousers and dresses in Milan",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2026/sep/22/skirts-miuccia-prada-raf-simons-milan-fashion-week",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T16:26:38.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "666ebdb98825857d",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Senior Iranian official indicates willingness to reopen strait of Hormuz if US takes steps to ease pressure on Tehran&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Iranian officials held three hours of talks with US special envoy Steve Witkoff on the sidelines of the UN general assembly, Donald Trump disclosed on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He said there would a further meeting in the very near future.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/iran-us-talks-sidelines-un-summit-trump-israel-us\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Iran and US have held talks on sidelines of UN summit, says Donald Trump",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/iran-us-talks-sidelines-un-summit-trump-israel-us",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T21:21:59.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bb9e84279bc33273",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;This live blog is now closed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tehran appears to have relaxed its preconditions for reopening the strait of Hormuz, saying it is prepared to do so within seven days so long as the US takes reciprocal steps to ease the pressure on Iran.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Previously Iran had set seven onerous pre-conditions for lifting the blockade including “an end to war on all fronts” and a commitment by the US to cease all aggressive actions against Iran including sanctions.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Middle East crisis: Trump says Iran will make a deal after US midterms – as it happened",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T19:09:42.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4d092944f78151fe",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Thousands flee fighting as Iran-aligned group seeks to consolidate territorial gains against Saudi-backed government forces&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates\"&gt;Middle East live – latest updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;As many as 169 people have been reportedly killed in Yemen in the last three days as Iran-aligned Houthis battle Saudi-backed government forces for control of strategic heights on the Red Sea coast, while thousands flee the violence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Houthi military officials said at least 118 people had been killed in clashes as well as Saudi air and artillery strikes on Taiz, al-Jawf, Marib and Saada provinces since Sunday, Agence France-Presse reported. Yemeni government sources have said at least 36 people have been killed on their side of the conflict.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/yemen-houthis-battle-strategic-red-sea-heights\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Up to 169 killed in Yemen as Houthis battle for Red Sea coastal heights",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/yemen-houthis-battle-strategic-red-sea-heights",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T13:57:36.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8aa4ab9dc6a6009e",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;MPs send out letter as Israeli government seeks bids for construction of large E1 settlement in West Bank&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;British banks and financial institutions are receiving written warnings from MPs that they should not invest in Israel’s E1 settlement project even though new UK laws banning trade with illegal settlements are unlikely to be in place for months.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A letter was sent to banks on Tuesday by the all-party Britain-Palestine group of MPs saying the onus was now on banks to review their obligations not to cooperate with new settlements.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/mps-uk-banks-investment-israeli-settlement-trade-ban\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "British banks warned not to invest in planned Israeli settlement before UK trade ban begins",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/mps-uk-banks-investment-israeli-settlement-trade-ban",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T13:43:41.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fbbcdaadd0e8fe60",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Andy Burnham seeks stability in Middle East to bring down prices at home as first meeting with Trump looms&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UK has agreed to provide defensive air support to Saudi Arabia to help counter Houthi fighters and restore stability in the Middle East while driving down the cost of living at home, Andy Burnham has said, ahead of his first meeting with Donald Trump.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The prime minister said he had agreed to a request for air-to-air refuelling of Saudi jets to defend energy infrastructure against the Iran-backed rebels and help keep oil flowing from the Gulf to ease global economic turmoil.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/21/uk-to-give-support-to-saudi-jets-in-attempt-to-counter-houthi-fighters\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "UK to give support to Saudi jets in attempt to counter Houthi fighters",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/21/uk-to-give-support-to-saudi-jets-in-attempt-to-counter-houthi-fighters",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T21:33:09.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "45ccc8302d61317a",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Islamic State-inspired bombings of churches and hotels in 2019 was one of the country’s worst ever attacks&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A court in Sri Lanka has convicted 15 men on terrorist charges for their involvement in the deadly &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/may/12/sri-lankan-catholic-churches-hold-first-sunday-services-since-easter-attacks\"&gt;2019 Easter bombings&lt;/a&gt; and sentenced them each to at least 220 years in prison.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The terror attacks, which targeted luxury hotels and churches as they held Easter services, left 267 people dead and wounded almost 6000. The bombings, which were inspired by Islamic State (IS), were among the deadliest attacks in Sri Lanka’s history and sent shockwaves through the country.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/sri-lanka-easter-bombings-15-sentenced-prison-terror-attacks\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Sri Lanka Easter bombings: 15 sentenced to hundreds of years in prison each over deadly terror attacks",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/sri-lanka-easter-bombings-15-sentenced-prison-terror-attacks",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T00:43:00.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "71bda500a2146572",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Generations of artisans from Mumbai to Lucknow have shaped the world’s most coveted designs. Plus, the gen Z memes giving classic Bollywood a new life&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Dior/videos/1339723023270765/\"&gt;zardozi embroidery&lt;/a&gt; on a Dior dress, the T-strap leather sandals at a Prada show, the mirror-work technique used on a Fendi bag – for decades, the skill of Indian artisans has been an invisible force behind some of the world’s most coveted fashion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now, that work is beginning to claim its own place in the spotlight, and the Mumbai-based textile and embroidery atelier &lt;a href=\"https://chanakya.in/\"&gt;Chanakya International&lt;/a&gt; is at the forefront.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/the-indian-craftsmanship-behind-luxury-fashion\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "‘What we have is unique’: the Indian craftsmanship behind global luxury fashion",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/the-indian-craftsmanship-behind-luxury-fashion",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T06:30:37.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "117277dd24e2b70f",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Police crack down on family and political supporters of former PM who say authorities are ‘slowly killing’ him in prison&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Three sisters of Pakistan’s incarcerated former prime minister Imran Khan have been arrested amid a heavy-handed government crackdown on plans for a nationwide protest to demand Khan’s release.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The lawyer for the three sisters, Aleema Khan, Uzma Khan and Noreen Niazi, said on Monday that they had all been detained and jailed for 30 days under a warrant that accused them of being a threat to public order.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/pakistan-jails-sisters-of-imran-khan-before-protest-seeking-his-release\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Pakistan jails sisters of Imran Khan before protest seeking his release",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/21/pakistan-jails-sisters-of-imran-khan-before-protest-seeking-his-release",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-21T14:48:49.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "66d6f9abeb241731",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Jagtar Singh Johal, from Scotland, was arrested after wedding in Punjab on alleged terrorism offences&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jagtar Singh Johal, a British Sikh man who was arrested in India in 2017 in connection with alleged terrorism offences, has been granted bail by a Delhi court.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Johal, from Scotland, was arrested for his alleged role in funding the Khalistan Liberation Force, which had carried out targeted killings in India’s Punjab region.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/18/british-sikh-man-granted-bail-in-india-nine-years-after-arrest\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "British Sikh man granted bail in India nine years after arrest",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/18/british-sikh-man-granted-bail-in-india-nine-years-after-arrest",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-18T13:02:44.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8e49f27a6ae995c2",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Mohammad Sharifullah, 28, was convicted of aiding the terrorist group that took credit for the suicide bombing &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An Islamic State group member was sentenced on Wednesday to 20 years in prison for aiding the terrorist organization that took credit for a suicide bombing that killed 13 US service members and about 160 Afghans at the Kabul airport five years ago during the US military’s chaotic withdrawal from the country.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A federal jury in Virginia had convicted Mohammad Sharifullah in April of providing material support to the IS affiliate known as Islamic State Khorasan Province (ISKP). But jurors could not agree whether he bore some responsibility for the airport bombing on 26 August 2021.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/is-member-sentenced-kabul-airport-bombing\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "IS member sentenced to 20 years in prison for role in 2021 Kabul airport bombing",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/is-member-sentenced-kabul-airport-bombing",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-17T13:40:30.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "854938245003a70d",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Exclusive: Restoration work at Bath Assembly Rooms unearths Roman ditches containing pottery, coins and fragments of a military helmet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The restoration of a Georgian building in Bath once frequented by Jane Austen has unexpectedly provided a tantalising glimpse into the life of the city’s Roman suburbanites.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A network of Roman ditches containing pottery, coins, glassware and a fragment of a military helmet has been found beneath &lt;a href=\"https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/bath-bristol/bath-assembly-rooms\"&gt;Bath Assembly Rooms&lt;/a&gt; in the north of the city.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/sep/23/archaeologists-clues-suburban-life-roman-times-bath\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Glimpses into lives of Roman suburbanites in Bath revealed in rare finds",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/sep/23/archaeologists-clues-suburban-life-roman-times-bath",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T06:00:19.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0e6fadb5fa76b4b7",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;In today’s newsletter: The PM’s first face‑to‑face with​ the US president marks a fragile reset&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Good morning. In the early hours of Tuesday a plane carrying Andy Burnham, a handful of UK ministers, an excited group of British political journalists, and Burnham’s wife, Marie France, landed at a New York airport for one of Burnham’s first major outings as prime minister: a face-to-face meeting with Donald Trump.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Considering the president once described Burnham as the mayor of “a town,” and the prime minister once said Trump wouldn’t be welcome in said town (Manchester), the meeting yesterday afternoon went remarkably well.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UN general assembly &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Donald Trump has called on nations to unite to isolate Tehran and bring down global energy prices, as he gave a bellicose &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/trump-calls-on-allies-enforce-complete-economic-isolation-iran-un-speech\"&gt;defence of his administration’s foreign policy&lt;/a&gt; and decision to strike Iran.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The far right &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Charities &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/far-right-activist-daniel-thomas-slashes-dinghy-with-blade-while-rescue-worker-onboard\"&gt;have condemned footage&lt;/a&gt; of a far-right activist using a blade to slash an inflatable dinghy in the Channel while a rescue worker was onboard, in a further escalation of organised anti-immigration protest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK news &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Children as young as 13 in the UK have been referred to a specialist clinic for a “devastating” bladder condition &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/sep/22/liverpool-alder-hey-hospital-rise-children-ketamine-bladder-addiction\"&gt;linked to sustained use of ketamine&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;West Bank &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| British banks and financial institutions are &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/mps-uk-banks-investment-israeli-settlement-trade-ban\"&gt;receiving warnings from MPs&lt;/a&gt; that they should not invest in Israel’s E1 settlement project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK politics &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Andy Burnham has opened the door to fighting the next election on the &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/andy-burnham-fails-rule-out-brexit-reversal-next-labour-manifesto\"&gt;UK rejoining the EU&lt;/a&gt;, but said his immediate priority was continuing to rebuild bridges with European allies.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/wednesday-briefing-can-burnham-seek-a-different-path-to-trumps-world-order\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Wednesday briefing: ​Can Burnham ​seek a ​different ​path​ to Trump’s world order?",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/wednesday-briefing-can-burnham-seek-a-different-path-to-trumps-world-order",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:45:26.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b9fd8215033869c9",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;PM aims to ‘stem poisonous tide’ of disinformation and deepfakes with National Centre for Information Defence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Security chiefs will set up a new national centre to tackle disinformation and deepfakes from hostile states such as Russia, Andy Burnham has announced, saying the government had a duty to “stem the poisonous tide” from damaging British interests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The National Centre for Information Defence will “detect, attribute and disrupt” information attacks by foreign powers, many of which are enabled by &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai\"&gt;AI&lt;/a&gt;, bringing together the intelligence agencies, law enforcement and social media companies.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/23/andy-burnham-national-centre-russian-disinformation-deepfakes\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "New UK agency to fight ‘information warfare’ from likes of Russia, Burnham tells UN",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/23/andy-burnham-national-centre-russian-disinformation-deepfakes",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:00:16.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "54f5fbc4df729b0b",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Treasury committee rejects calls for fundamental reform of independent watchdog the Office for Budget Responsibility&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Attacks on the government’s independent economic forecaster from left and right of the political spectrum are akin to “shooting the messenger”, according to an influential group of MPs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Treasury committee rejected “siren calls to fundamentally reform” the Office for Budget Responsibility (OBR) and said it should not be blamed when policymakers had to make tough decisions because of tight public finances.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/23/obr-treasury-committee-shooting-messenger-mps-economic-forecaster-uk\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Critics of UK government’s economic forecaster are ‘shooting the messenger’, say MPs",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/23/obr-treasury-committee-shooting-messenger-mps-economic-forecaster-uk",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:00:16.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4b6ad16a7bf986f8",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;‘Radical’ report likely to influence party’s platform also proposes abolishing inheritance and capital gains taxes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A thinktank linked to Reform UK has called for the abolition of the state pension and £75bn worth of sweeping tax cuts in a “radical” report likely to influence the party’s platform for the next election.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=\"https://www.cfabb.uk/how-we-work\"&gt;Centre for a Better Britain’s (CFABB)&lt;/a&gt; report – which also calls for weaker rules for UK banks and Trump-style investment accounts offering £1,000 to newborns – will be formally launched at a private event with City executives on Wednesday.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/23/thinktank-reform-uk-abolition-state-pension\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Thinktank linked to Reform UK calls for abolition of state pension",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/23/thinktank-reform-uk-abolition-state-pension",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T04:00:15.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f72b83de4e095313",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;This live blog is now closed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;amp;utm_content=signup&amp;amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\"&gt;Sign up for US Breaking News emails&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trump&lt;/strong&gt; is arriving at the UN HQ right now.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After &lt;em&gt;very&lt;/em&gt; brief doorstep comments – almost exclusively &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/21/trump-tv-networks-white-house-pool-coverage\"&gt;mocking CNN&lt;/a&gt; - he answers a reporter’s &lt;em&gt;very loud &lt;/em&gt;question by saying his message to Putin is: “settle the war.”&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/sep/22/donald-trump-unga-speech-iran-middle-east-ukraine-latest-news-updates\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Trump defends actions in Iran and Venezuela in UN General Assembly address amid rising tensions with allies – as it happened",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/sep/22/donald-trump-unga-speech-iran-middle-east-ukraine-latest-news-updates",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T01:48:22.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e8657b7a56bd8b6a",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Surrogate who rejected abortion request had asked justices to halt court order recognizing LA couple as legal parents&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The supreme court has refused to get involved with a custody dispute between an Alaska surrogate and a California couple whose child was born with a rare and serious heart defect.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On Tuesday, Justice Elena Kagan denied an emergency request from McKenna West, an Alaska nurse and surrogate who had &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/12/surrogate-mother-texas-custody-supreme-court-appeal\"&gt;asked &lt;/a&gt;the US’s highest court to halt a California court order recognizing the couple, Omar Ahmed and Nausheen Gilkar, as the boy’s legal parents.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/supreme-court-surrogate-custody-battle\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "US supreme court declines to intervene in custody fight over baby born via surrogate",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/supreme-court-surrogate-custody-battle",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T22:38:28.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1dc09892f9530b81",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Former VP, who lost state to Trump in 2024 elections, is lending her popularity to unite fractured party&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kamala Harris returned to Michigan on Tuesday to campaign for Abdul El-Sayed, lending her popularity among Black voters to a progressive Senate nominee still working to unite a party fractured by a bruising primary – and the former vice-president’s loss to Donald Trump in the state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Appearing with El-Sayed at a Detroit birth center, Harris used a roundtable on Black maternal health to frame that November’s contest against the Republican Mike Rogers as a fight over women’s access to care.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/kamala-harris-abdul-el-sayed-campaign-michigan\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Kamala Harris returns to Michigan to campaign for Abdul El-Sayed for Senate",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/kamala-harris-abdul-el-sayed-campaign-michigan",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T22:18:18.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a5f71411a3931588",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;US officials have begun to buy back wind leases as president seek to block renewables in favor of fossil fuels&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Democratic attorneys general from California and New York have sued the Trump administration over its plans to buy back offshore wind leases as Donald Trump seeks to discourage the expansion of wind energy in favor of fossil fuels.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;California attorney general Rob Bonta said he was suing over removal of a project off his state’s coast planned by Chicago-based Invenergy. The Trump administration said in June it was buying back the company’s US offshore wind leases for four wind projects on the east and west coasts.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/california-new-york-trump-wind-energy\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "California and New York sue over Trump push to halt wind energy projects",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/california-new-york-trump-wind-energy",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T21:35:42.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a498e053c52c25cc",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;The park is the most highly visited and strong winds make trash problem worse, with gusts blowing away items&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hold on to your hats – Yellowstone national park staffers &lt;a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/observatories/yvo/news/caps-trash-and-other-hydrothermal-funky-finds-2026-edition\"&gt;have removed&lt;/a&gt; a record-setting 20,100 pieces of trash from hydrothermal areas around the geyser-filled park so far this year&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The most commonly found items include 280 hats, 54 camera lens caps, 47 hair ties, 42 pencils, 36 pairs of sunglasses, 20 hotel key cards and 17 baby pacifiers.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/yellowstone-trash-record\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Hats, pencils and baby pacifiers: Yellowstone staffers retrieve record amount of trash from hot springs",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/yellowstone-trash-record",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-22T20:46:15.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    }
